 {"id":"fabro-0863","title":"Engine: RunCreated constructor at the RunSpec seam — four hand-built sites become one constructor","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-10T07:14:04.654Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T07:14:04.654Z","description":"Architecture review 2026-09-10 (improve-codebase-architecture). Entry-level companion to the lifecycle-protocol seed; purely mechanical.\n\nPROBLEM: Event::RunCreated is hand-assembled at four sites — operations/create.rs:556-585, operations/retry.rs:68-93, operations/fork.rs:158-183, fabro-workflow test_support.rs:206-231 — each serializing settings/graph itself and threading ~24 fields individually. A new mandatory RunCreated field breaks four places; each site re-derives what persist_created_run already knows.\n\nWANTED: One constructor at the RunSpec seam, e.g. RunSpec::into_created_event(title, provenance_overrides, retried_from, parent_id, web_url) in fabro-types records.rs (upstream churn there: 0/12w). create/retry/fork/test_support call it with their deltas; serialization lives inside the constructor.\n\nDRIFT RULES: additive; exactly one call-site edit each in create.rs (upstream-identical, churn 35/12w) and fork.rs (churn 13/12w) — keep surgical, no reformatting beyond the call.\n\nACCEPTANCE: parity check that emitted event bytes are identical before/after (snapshot); a deliberately added mandatory field breaks exactly one place; retry/fork/create test fixtures shrink (no per-site 24-field building).\n\nBASIS: commit bfbe3a6c8 (2026-09-09); /tmp/arch-walk-store-workflow.md (F1).","labels":["engine","architecture"]}
 {"id":"fabro-ab8e","title":"Fork footprint: extract fork additions out of upstream-churn hot files (tests.rs, automation_scheduler.rs)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-10T07:14:04.741Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T07:14:04.741Z","description":"Architecture review 2026-09-10. Cross-cutting fork-strategy seed — runs alongside the other architecture seeds (lifecycle protocol, typed admission) whose modules are natural extraction targets.\n\nPROBLEM: Fork additions live physically inside upstream's hottest files. server/tests.rs carries +2083 fork-added lines while upstream churns it 112 commits/12w (worst ratio in the repo); automation_scheduler.rs is +555/1433 (~40% fork code, churn 13/12w); server.rs +279 (churn 49/12w). Every upstream merge pays conflict hunks on fork lines that have no locality of their own. The target pattern already exists and is proven: server/handler/wait.rs and tests/it/api/run_wait.rs are fork-owned files.\n\nWANTED: Move fork-added tests into fork-owned test files; extract fork scheduler/materializer logic into fork-owned modules (prefer interfaces delivered by the lifecycle/admission seeds); upstream files keep only registration and call-site lines. Moves only — no behavior change, no test deletions.\n\nACCEPTANCE: fork test count unchanged (moves, verified by count); fork additions greppable from fork-owned files; the next upstream merge shows measurably fewer conflicted hunks in tests.rs and automation_scheduler.rs (record the diff in the close note).\n\nBASIS: commit bfbe3a6c8 (2026-09-09); drift data from git diff --numstat upstream/main..HEAD and git log churn on upstream/main (12w); review card K7, /tmp/architecture-review-20260910-090054.html.","labels":["engine","architecture"]}
 {"id":"fabro-27dc","title":"engine: conductor parks at soft exit after Work-routed survey since the 2026-09-09 22:29 deploy - develop leg never starts (line down)","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":0,"createdAt":"2026-09-10T07:41:32.446Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-10T08:17:14.940Z","description":"LINE DOWN INCIDENT 2026-09-10 07:01-09:30 (line-watch, reproduced twice): after the night deploy (server image built 2026-09-09 22:29 CEST, container started 22:35), every conductor pass parks at the soft exit immediately after a Work-routed survey; the develop leg never starts.\n\nEvidence:\n- Automation-fired pass 01M251VFNABCNMA94QDNHYZ5Q7 (07:00-07:01) and manual repair fire 01M253EWK1X299DRFTAJJHA0MV (07:28-07:29) both: survey stage completes green with correct route decision journaled ('route decision: Work'), then the exit handler completes in 0ms and run.failed fires with reason=soft_stop, kind=soft, category=deterministic (\"infrastructure could not finish\"). No develop-leg journal entry, no child run created.\n- stage.completed context_values carry NO preferred_next_label on EITHER the broken passes or the last-known-good pass (20:08 yesterday on the OLD image) - routing reads the structured output elsewhere; do not chase the context key.\n- Last known-good conductor pass on the previous image: 01M23W3067KQ 20:08-21:10 (develop child 01M23W4S7Q2G created fine, PR #113).\n- The deployed image contains the 2026-09-09 engine merges: #84 (allow-keys lint), #90/fabro-91ff (overlap guard: run_summary_store + planner/analyze prompts), #96/fabro-de4d (preferred_label edge validation in fabro-validate, new rule routing_fallback_silent), #99/fabro-94e8 (update-branch), #107+#109 (PR postlude). Prime suspects: routing/output-schema handling around de4d and 91ff.\n- Secondary blocker: the automation breaker (signature park|Conductor|soft_stop, consecutive_count 1, threshold appears to be 1) suppresses the */30 schedule after the first soft_stop - even a one-off park kills the line until the breaker resets.\n\nRepro: FABRO_SERVER=http://localhost:32276 just run conductor (twice, deterministic). Also note the local repair path tripped over auth.json URL keying (127.0.0.1 vs localhost entry) - separate papercut.\n\nExpected fix: find why the survey->develop edge (condition preferred_label=\"Work\") is not taken on the new image though the survey emits the route; also revisit the breaker threshold (a single soft_stop should not permanently suppress the schedule without an incident signal).\n\nExecution note: filed by line-watch during line-down; the line cannot pick this up itself (chicken-egg) - direct agent repair with user knowledge, or user-led. ROOT CAUSE FOUND (line-watch 10:2x, inspect of 01M253EWK1X): the survey agent's final answer literally set preferred_next_label=\"Unrouted survey outcome\" (last_response in the stage context: {\"preferred_next_label\":\"Unrouted survey outcome\",\"outcome\":\"succeeded\",...}) while its journal says 'route decision: Work'. The engine's Edge selected log confirms: from survey to exit label=\"Unrouted survey outcome\" reason=\"preferred_label\". fabro-de4d (#96, in the 22:29 image) constrains the routing output_schema enum from the node's outgoing edges - but the survey's outgoing set includes the UNCONDITIONAL safety-net edge (validator rule all_conditional_edges, label \"Unrouted survey outcome\"), so the fallback became a first-class valid choice and glm-5.3 picks it deterministically (2/2 passes on the new image). FIX DIRECTION: build the preferred_label enum from CONDITIONAL choice edges only (exclude unconditional safety nets and outcome=failed edges) in the de4d schema construction (lib/components/fabro-workflow, routing/output_schema area); optionally also make the model-facing schema description mark the fallback as engine-reserved. The old image worked because the enum was not edge-constrained. FIXED 2026-09-10 10:5x (line-watch direct repair, mandate: line down): lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/handler/structured_output.rs routable_edge_labels now includes conditional edges whose condition routes on preferred_label naming the label (clause walk incl. and/or/not); regression tests cover the conductor-survey shape and composite conditions. Verification: cargo test -p fabro-workflow --lib (2 new tests green, 1326 pass; 4 pipeline failures pre-exist on clean tree - sandbox/env-dependent), clippy + fmt on touched crate green (nightly-2026-04-14). Commit 0373f5c10; deployed via just up.","labels":["engine","workflows"],"assignee":"agent"}
